import json,pathlib,random
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
rows='''1~Which statement about a high-level river-dispute committee is sound?~Consultation can support cooperation without itself replacing lawful adjudication.~It automatically repeals Article262.|It proves the2019amendmentBillhas become law.|It changes the Tungabhadra into a left-bank tributary of the Krishna.~Negotiation,tribunal jurisdiction and project operations are distinct. A magazine’s recommendation to implement aBillis not proof it was enacted.
2~Which is the newly added component in the reviewedDISHA2.0framework?~VIDHI-Sanjeevani.~Abolition of all legal-aid eligibility rules.|A guarantee of a favourable judgment.|An ordinance replacing every court with a chatbot.~The fourth component adds digital monitoring and multilingual assistance; it does not replace courts,qualified counsel or the conditions for representation.
4~The5JuneGDPprovisional release reports real growth of:~7.7%forFY2025–26on base2022–23.~7.9%forGDPbecauseGDPandGVAare always identical.|8.9%realGDPbecause nominal means constant prices.|7.7%only for the month ofJune.~Annual realGDP7.7%,nominal8.9%,realGVA7.9%andQ4realGDP7.8%refer to different concepts or periods.
4~Why can one not infer a sector’s absolute growth contribution from its growth rate alone?~The sector’s initial weight/size also matters.~All sectors have equal weights by definition.|A10.7%manufacturing rate means manufacturing is10.7%ofGDP.|Every fast-growing sector must account for most output.~A sector growing rapidly from a small base can contribute less absolute output than a larger slower-growing sector.
5~The5Junepolicy decision and19Junedocument are best described as:~The MPCdecision and its later-published minutes.~Two separate rate cuts.|A state lending decision followed by aUnionBudget.|A meeting beginning19Juneand ending5June.~The reviewed minutes explicitly describe the3–5Junemeeting and publish its unchanged-rate resolution on19June.
5~A neutral stance with a5.25%repo means:~Policy remains data-dependent without a predetermined next move.~A compulsory cut at the next meeting.|SDFmust be higher thanMSF.|Inflation has necessarily fallen to zero.~The reviewed corridor remainsSDF5.00%,repo5.25%,MSF5.50%.Neutrality is not a promise of easing.
6~Which set correctly distinguishesQ4FY2025–26external-account flows?~Net secondary income+US$41.3billion;gross personal transfersUS$43.5billion.~Both areUS$30.1billionby definition.|Primary income+US$41.3billionand services−US$60.4billion.|The current-account surplus proves goods exports exceeded imports.~TheRBIprimary table distinguishes net secondary income,gross personal-transfer receipts and primary-income outgo. Services/transfers cushion the goods deficit.
6~AUS$7.1billionQ4current-account surplus proves that:~That quarter had a surplus,not necessarily the financial year.~FY2025–26had no current-account deficit.|Foreign portfolio inflows were necessarily positive.|Merchandise trade was in surplus.~The full-year preliminary current account was aUS$25.2billiondeficit,0.6%ofGDP,despite theQ4surplus.
7~The5JuneIncome-taxOrdinanceis deemed effective from:~1April2026.~1January2027because allJuneinstruments share one commencement.|Only the first sale of a corporate bond by any citizen.|The nextMPCmeeting.~The full Gazette specifies deemed1Aprilcommencement and a government-security exemption forFIIsandBISsubject to prescribed information.
8~Under the reviewed individual portfolio route,the relevant individual threshold is:~Below10%.~Exactly10%without any reclassification consequence.|24%for every individual by right.|100%without beneficial-owner scrutiny.~The individual and aggregate thresholds differ:below10%and24%respectively. Ownership/control and other safeguards remain relevant.
9~Under theJunefinancial-sales directions,signed consent:~Does not make an unsuitable sale appropriate.~Eliminates all mis-selling risk by definition.|Allows a defaultYeschoice online.|Requires a customer to buy every product listed.~The inspected definition recognises mis-selling even with explicit consent where suitability/appropriateness is absent. The default consent choice must beNo.
10~The newJune24digital-fraud rules apply to the specified transactions undertaken:~On or after1January2027.~Automatically from1June2026.|Only before the notification date.|Only if Parliament holds anMPCmeeting.~Issue date and operative transaction date differ. The primary commercial-bank directions expressly use1January2027.
10~For reviewed third-party breaches,the five-day zero-liability reporting clock runs:~In calendar days from occurrence.~In working days after the victim reads anSMS.|Only after a criminal conviction.|From the next annual audit.~The customer must notify the bank within five calendar days of occurrence for that category; bank negligence has a distinct zero-liability rule.
11~An eligible victim loses₹40,000gross and recovers₹15,000before compensation. The amount is:~₹21,250.~₹34,000.|₹25,000always.|₹40,000plus₹25,000.~Net loss is₹25,000;85%is₹21,250,below the₹25,000cap. Eligibility and reporting conditions still apply.
11~Which pair of limits is preserved in the reviewed small-fraud mechanism?~Once in a lifetime and qualifying losses within the specified one-year effective-date window.~One claim every day and no end date.|Unlimited claims if each is₹50,000.|A₹50,000minimum loss and compensation equal to85%ofgrosswithout recoveries.~The rule uses gross loss up to₹50,000for eligibility,net loss for calculation,and separate lifetime/window limits.
12~The reviewed liquidation time limits are:~180daysfor liquidation and15daysfor distribution after receipt.~15daysfor all insolvency resolution and180daysbefore acknowledging every payment.|One year and90daysunchanged.|180yearsand15months.~The inspected English amendment changes the earlier one-year liquidation and90-daydistribution periods. These clocks do not guarantee full recovery or remove extension procedures.
13~The ATFstabilisation corpus is primarily:~A recoverable interest-free advance toOMCsunder a price-smoothing arrangement.~An unconditional cash grant to every airline passenger.|Cancellation of every airline loan.|A new permanent state tax payable only inAP.~The mechanism supports willing scheduled carriers and recovers differential amounts as prices moderate,with monitoring and annual review.
14~Which chronology is supported by the inspected laterMoSPIrelease?~1JunenewIIPseries;29JunePPI-based supersession.~28Mayactual launch merely because it was scheduled.|29Junefirst-ever industrial index inIndia.|1Juneand29Juneare the same release date.~A scheduled date,actual new-series launch and later methodological supersession are different milestones.
16~Under the draftAAYformula,a three-person household would receive:~21kgper month,subject to the proposed scheme conditions.~35kgplus21kg.|49kgwithout a cap.|5kgfor the household.~The draft uses7kgper person with maximum35kgper household; current reviewedAAYlaw remains household-based until valid amendment/commencement.
16~The draftAAYformula’s implication for a seven-person family is:~The35kghousehold ceiling still applies.~49kgis guaranteed because7times7is49.|The cap disappears above five persons.|It proves Parliament enacted the draft.~The cap prevents a simple uncapped per-person entitlement. Consultation is not enactment; the potential distributional effect needs scrutiny.
19~Why isGPStracking alone insufficient for an ambulance system?~Triage,trained staff,appropriate destinations and clinical handover also matter.~Every nearest building is necessarily a trauma centre.|A vehicle location automatically proves patient survival.|The guidelines immediately certify all state fleets.~NASincludes standards,dispatch,GISplanning and pre-hospital care. Announcing a framework is not proof of universal compliance.
26~TheAntarcticTreaty’s65-year milestone in2026marks:~Entry into force on23June1961.~Signature on23June1961.|Automatic expiry of theMadridProtocol.|Creation of a territorial claim byIndia.~The Treaty was signed1December1959; entry into force was23June1961. Treaty layers and claim rules must be distinguished.
28~A credible biochar assessment must consider:~Feedstock,production emissions,soil response and carbon persistence.~Only the wordbioin its name.|A universal guaranteed30%yield increase.|Automatic permanent sequestration with no monitoring.~Potential benefits are context-dependent. Pyrolysis differs from full combustion and lifecycle accounting matters.
29~Coral bleaching necessarily means:~Stress and loss of symbionts/pigment,but not immediate inevitable death.~The coral is a plant that has permanently died.|The reef has become immune to warming.|Ocean warming is the only possible stressor.~Bleached corals may recover if conditions improve; prolonged stress can cause mortality. Resilience is not invulnerability.
35~The28JuneATLASbriefing is based on:~Oxygen/neon collision data recorded in2025.~The first-ever oxygen collision conducted28June2026.|Creation of stable room-temperatureQGPfuel.|Proof every proton collision produces identical effects.~Publication date differs from data-taking. Jet quenching is inferred through measured particle-jet momentum imbalance and comparisons across centrality.
36~WHO’sJuneoutbreak update cautions that newly reported cases:~May reflect a testing backlog rather than newly acquired infections.~Always equal infections acquired the same day.|Make confirmed-case fatality identical to infection fatality.|Prove sustained community transmission in every country visited.~Reporting,diagnosis and infection dates differ. The historicalJuneupdate also must not be presented as currentNovembercounts.
46~AP’sAviationPolicy2026–31and reported2035capacity targets are:~A policy period and a separate target horizon.~Proof every target is achieved by2031.|A record of airports already operating.|A guarantee all proposed routes are commercially viable.~Approval,planned capacity,actual traffic and operating viability require separate evidence.
49~A₹300crorestate guarantee for the reviewedFiberNetfinancing is:~A contingent fiscal exposure,not an immediate grant to every household.~The same as two separate₹300crorecash grants.|Proof₹300croreofnewfibreis already commissioned.|A waiver of the borrower’s repayment duty.~The reported borrower,guarantor and intended fund user differ. Loans,guarantees and grants should not be double-counted.
53~An invitation to bid for theAmaravatiEyeunderDBFOTestablishes:~A procurement stage,not an awarded operating concession.~That construction and safety certification are complete.|That private finance eliminates all public fiscal risk.|That every public riverbank is available without clearance.~Design,Build,Finance,OperateandTransferdescribes a contract model. Selection,agreement,construction and operation remain distinct.
55~Seven lakhconstructionman-daysper year means:~An estimated amount of labour time,not seven lakhpermanent jobs.~Seven lakhpersons guaranteed lifelong employment.|Seven lakhcompleted central offices.|₹7lakhcroreofwages.~The official capital-project account uses man-days,an employment-time unit. Cost approvals and completed expenditure are also distinct.'''
Q=[];rng=random.Random(13)
for row in rows.splitlines():
 i,q,right,wrong,e=row.split('~');opts=[right]+wrong.split('|');assert len(opts)==4; rng.shuffle(opts)
 Q.append(dict(id=f'JUN26-{len(Q)+1:02}',question=q,options=opts,answer=opts.index(right),explanation=e,ref=f'E13-2606-{int(i):03}'))
assert len(Q)==30,len(Q)
(R/'data/2026-06-mcqs.json').write_text(json.dumps(Q,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
